    {
      "id": "s1q1",
      "number": 1,
      "section": "A",
      "standard": "S1.a",
      "difficulty": "medium",
      "type": "simplify",
      "question_html": "Let \\( f(x) = 2x^3 - 4x^2 + 3x - 1 \\) and \\( g(x) = x^3 + 5x^2 - 2x + 4 \\).<br>Find \\( f(x) + g(x) \\). Write your answer in standard form.",
      "inputs": [
        {
          "id": "s1q1_ans",
          "type": "text",
          "label": "Answer =",
          "answer": "3x^3 + x^2 + x + 3",
          "normalize": "poly"
        }
      ],
      "hint": "Add like terms for each degree: x³ terms, x² terms, x terms, and constants separately.",
      "solution_html": "\\( (2x^3 + x^3) + (-4x^2 + 5x^2) + (3x - 2x) + (-1 + 4) = 3x^3 + x^2 + x + 3 \\)"
    },
    {
      "id": "s1q2",
      "number": 2,
      "section": "A",
      "standard": "S1.a",
      "difficulty": "medium",
      "type": "simplify",
      "question_html": "Let \\( f(x) = 3x^3 + 2x^2 - 5x + 1 \\) and \\( g(x) = x^3 - 4x^2 + 3x - 6 \\).<br>Find \\( f(x) - g(x) \\). Write your answer in standard form.",
      "inputs": [
        {
          "id": "s1q2_ans",
          "type": "text",
          "label": "Answer =",
          "answer": "2x^3 + 6x^2 - 8x + 7",
          "normalize": "poly"
        }
      ],
      "hint": "Distribute the negative sign to every term of g(x) first, then combine like terms.",
      "solution_html": "\\( (3x^3 - x^3) + (2x^2 + 4x^2) + (-5x - 3x) + (1 + 6) = 2x^3 + 6x^2 - 8x + 7 \\)"
    },
    {
      "id": "s1q4",
